7. Order of work, each step only after the one before passed:
   - the board's strict scan, `viola_state::board::scan`, before anything is opened: a refusal is exit 21, the home or
     instance pair (or under `--json` `{"v":1,"error":"instance-unreachable","detail":"strict-modes-failed"}`), no log,
     no line (`viola list`'s ratified rule);
   - under a parsed `VIOLA_NAME` only, the caller's `cli` log opened through `client::start`, as `list` does (T5);
   - the boot time read once (`boot_time`); `None` → nothing is selected by the boot rule (every instance reads
     not-taken), stated on stderr by one fixed `unable:` / `hint:` pair and exit 1 — a host that hides its boot time is
     not guessed at;
   - per scanned instance, in name order, the snapshot through `read_snapshot_or_replay` ONCE (its `state-recovered`
     line as `list` writes it) and the liveness `classify`: `Live` → `already-live`, `Stale` → `stale-heartbeat`
     (both skipped, both exit-0 outcomes); `Gone` → a candidate when `beat_before` the boot and either it was named,
     or `ended_after_last_start` is false; a named instance that is not a candidate reads `not-taken`; an unnamed one
     is left out silently;
   - per candidate: `session_chain`'s newest session-shaped id, else `no-session`; a real snapshot whose `cwd` is a
     directory, else `cwd-missing` (revive's own readings, read ahead so the line can name them);
   - ONE `claude agents --json` read for the whole set (`run::agents::read_here`), a candidate whose newest id it lists
     reading `session-live`; a failed read passes (fail-open, as revive's);
   - the order: parents first over the candidates, `lineage.parent` naming another candidate as the edge, a parent
     naming none a root, a cycle taken once from its first name in name order — the board's `forest` rule
     (src/human/board/rows.rs:20-40) applied to the candidate set; the parent read only to order, never joined into a
     path (security-plan · decision/lineage-parent-authenticates-nothing);
   - `--dry-run`: every candidate that passed reads `would-open`; nothing is spawned; exit 0.

14. A pre-reboot fleet is produced by running viola, never written by hand (tests S2): each instance started through
    `viola open` over the stand-in `foot` and `hyprctl` (a recorded window and workspace) or through `run` (no window:
    hand-started), its parent declared; each wrapper ended by `kill_wrapper` (tests/support/start.rs); then its
    heartbeat mtime set before the host's boot time — the one hand-made change, as `tests/cli_revive.rs`'s `age_beat`
    sets one (tests/cli_revive.rs:91-98). Every spawned terminal and its tree ended by a drop guard reading
    `foot-spawns.ndjson`'s pids, `tests/cli_open.rs`'s `Terminal` pattern per spawn. Cases, each a literal oracle on the
    contract:
    - `up_reopens_each_pre_boot_instance_parents_first` — a parent and its child (child sorted first by name): the
      spawn order in `foot-spawns.ndjson` is parent then child; each argv the closed argv of step 9 (`revive <name>
      --origin cli`); each instance's events from its revived start's offset hold `wheel{driver,start}`, `lineage`,
      `launch`, `window` and `session-start` with source `resume` and the logged id; the lines read
      `<name>  live  placed`;
    - `up_moves_each_window_to_its_recorded_workspace` — the `hyprctl-asked` receipts hold one move per placed
      instance to its recorded workspace, on that terminal's own window;
    - `up_opens_a_hand_started_instance_unplaced` — no recorded window: no move, `live  unplaced`;
    - `up_skips_a_live_and_a_stale_instance` — one wrapper live, one frozen (`Frozen`, tests/support/frozen.rs): lines
      `already-live` and `stale-heartbeat`, no spawn, exit 0;
    - `up_leaves_out_an_instance_ended_on_purpose_or_this_boot` — one whose log ends in `session-end` (a clean `/exit`
      over the fake), one whose beat is after the boot time: neither spawned nor printed; the named form takes the
      first (`viola up <it>`) and prints `not-taken` for the second;
    - `up_names_no_session_cwd_missing_and_session_live` — each a line, no spawn for it, exit 1, the rest of the fleet
      still re-opened;
    - `up_dry_run_prints_the_plan_and_spawns_nothing` — `would-open` lines in order, no `foot-spawns.ndjson`;
    - `up_json_is_one_document_of_closed_words`;
    - `up_refuses_a_home_another_user_may_read_with_no_line` — exit 21, the pair, no log, no line, mode as found;
    - `up_without_foot_refuses_terminal_not_found_and_spawns_nothing`;
    - `up_writes_neither_snapshot_nor_stamps` — over a fleet of only live instances, `snapshot.json` and `stamps.json`
      byte-identical.

