   - the stand-in's `fake-args` also carry `--trusted-root <root>/work`, so `--screens` draws no trust form;
   - its `agents-mode` is `malformed`, since every stand-in session holds the one recorded session id. The second
     revive would otherwise read the first as `session-live`. `tests/cli_up.rs` does the same, outside its
     `session-live` case;
   - each instance's one `viola send` is made and its exit is in no verdict, because the stand-in logs its session at
     launch.

